<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Georges Danton</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1759–1794</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Georges Jacques Danton</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Georges Danton was a lawyer and orator who became one of the leading figures of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/french-revolution">French Revolution</a>. A founder of the Cordeliers Club, he was minister of justice after the fall of the monarchy in 1792 and rallied the nation against foreign invasion. A member of the first <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/committee-of-public-safety">Committee of Public Safety</a>, he later urged moderation and an end to the Terror, and was tried and executed in April 1794 on the orders of the faction around Robespierre.</p></div>
